  <data name="StatusHoldToConfirmHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>In the Unit and Responder apps, crews press and hold a status button for two seconds to set it, instead of tapping it and then pressing Next or Submit. Prevents accidental taps and forgotten confirmations. A status that needs a note or a destination choice still opens its next step.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CloseCallWhenUnitsClearLabel" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Close call when last unit clears</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CloseCallWhenUnitsClearHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>An active call closes on its own when the last unit dispatched to it reports back in service or out of service (a status whose base type is Available, In Quarters, Cleared, Unavailable or Maintenance). Every other dispatched unit must also have reported finished since its dispatch. Only units count: a call with no unit dispatched, a call under an active incident command, or a unit still returning or transporting keeps the call open for the dispatcher.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberingHeader" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Call Numbering</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberingIntro" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>How new calls are numbered. Changing the pattern never renumbers calls that already have a number.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberPattern" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Call number pattern</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberExample" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Example:</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberPatternHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Fixed text (letters, digits, - _ . /) around tokens: {YYYY} or {YY} the year, {MM} the month, {DD} the day and {SEQ} the sequence, which must appear once. The sequence starts again at 1 whenever the date in the number changes: each year with a year, each month with {MM}, each day with {DD}, and never without a date. {MM} needs a year and {DD} needs {MM}. Dates use the department's time zone.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberSequenceWidth" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Sequence digits</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberSequenceWidthHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Pads the sequence with leading zeros, so 4 writes 0153. 1 writes it without padding, as Resgrid always has.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberNext" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Next call number</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberResetsYearly" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Starts again at 1 each year.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberResetsMonthly" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Starts again at 1 each month.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberResetsDaily" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Starts again at 1 each day.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberResetsNever" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Never starts again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberRaiseTo" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Raise next sequence to</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberRaiseToHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>For departments continuing numbers issued before Resgrid: the next call receives this sequence. It can only be raised, never lowered, so a number is never issued twice. Leave it blank to keep the current sequence.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberRaiseConfirm" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Raise the next call number? It can only be raised, never lowered.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberPatternInvalid" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The call numbering was not saved. The pattern needs {SEQ} exactly once, can only contain letters, digits, - _ . / and the {YYYY}, {YY}, {MM} and {DD} tokens, needs a year for {MM} and {MM} for {DD}, and can be at most 40 characters.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberNextBelowCurrent" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The next call number was not raised: it can only be raised above the number the next call already receives ({0}).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberNextPatternChanged" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The next call number was not raised because the pattern or the numbering year start changed in the same save. Raise it again for the new sequence.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberYearStart" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Numbering year starts</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberYearStartDay" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Day of the month</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberYearLabelEndYear" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Named by the year it ends in</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberYearLabelStartYear" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Named by the year it starts in</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberYearStartHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>For calls numbered by a fiscal year, pick the day it starts. A yearly pattern starts again at 1 that day, and {YYYY} and {YY} write the fiscal year's name. Most fiscal years are named by the year they end in, so one starting November 1, 2026 is 2027. January 1 is the calendar year. Patterns with {MM} or {DD} always follow the calendar.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberResetsYearlyOn" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Starts again at 1 each year on {0}.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="CallNumberYearStartInvalid" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The call numbering was not saved. The numbering year has to start on a day every year has, so February 29 cannot be used.</value>
  </data>
