  <data name="DocumentNumberingIntro" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>How Resgrid numbers work orders, invoices, bids and daily time reports. Leave a pattern blank to keep the built-in numbers. Changing a pattern never renumbers documents that already have a number, and a new pattern carries on after any number it would repeat.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DocumentNumberingRecordsLink" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Records numbering</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DocumentNumberingYearStartHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>For documents numbered by a fiscal year, pick the day it starts. Work order numbers, and patterns with a year, start again at 1 that day, and {YYYY} and {YY} write the fiscal year's name. Most fiscal years are named by the year they end in, so one starting November 1, 2026 is 2027. January 1 is the calendar year. Call and Records numbers have their own year start.</value>
  </data>
